2,4$ 2c : Dermatocystidia multiseptate, smooth or diverticulate, spores with projecting isolated spines, rarely forming a reticulum.

3,6$ 3a : Found under Betula, fruit bodies fleshy, at least medium-sized, pileus red, orange-red or partially yellow, lamellae crowded, spore print dark yellow, context almost unchanging, spores small, often rounded. $ Series Lundellii. $s"Series Lundellii."
3,7$ 3b : Dermatocystidia clavate, non septate, spores small or medium-sized, partially reticulate, spore print IVc to IVe, context turning grey in typical forms, rarely slightly yellowing. $ Series Decipiens. $s"Series Decipiens."

